# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# promptless — per-user runtime state
#
# These files are regenerated on every use and differ between machines.
# Committing them would leak per-user session data, cause constant diff
# noise, and force contributors into each other's conversation context.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# opencode session persistence
# ------------------------------
# Created automatically in each project root to persist the current
# opencode session ID so the next prompt resumes the same conversation.
# Sessions are per-user, per-machine — committing this would let anyone
# who clones the repo resume *your* session.
.promptless-session
.promptless-session.*

# Editor and tool runtime directories
# ------------------------------------
# These directories contain per-user, per-machine session state,
# preferences, caches, and conversation histories.  They are regenerated
# on every use and should never be committed: they differ between
# contributors, contain potentially sensitive session traces, and would
# produce constant diff noise.
.opencode/
.commandcode/
.claude/
